== Header + section framing, bytes per second per player (design §4.1, §5.2, §6.2)
profile  dir   design   proposed  saved
busy     up     886.2     352.5   533.8 (60.2%)
busy     dn     352.5     130.0   222.5 (63.1%)
idle     up     115.0      71.2    43.8 (38.0%)
idle     dn     135.0     100.0    35.0 (25.9%)

== Upstream unreliable input frame, bytes (design: tick+ack+bits+seq+tag+section)
design header 12.88 B vs input payload 6.5-9.0 B/packet [state-sync §4.1]
proposed header 4.25 B (no new ack) / 7.75 B (with ack)

== Ack repetition: how many upstream acks cover each downstream unreliable frame
bitfield L  dn_u Hz  ack frames/s  repeats  P(never acked | 5% iid loss)
        8       20            20      9.0  2.0e-12
        8       20            10      4.5  1.4e-06
        8       60            10      1.5  1.1e-02
        8       60            60      9.0  2.0e-12
       16       20            20     17.0  7.6e-23
       16       20            10      8.5  8.7e-12
       16       60            10      2.8  2.1e-04
       16       60            60     17.0  7.6e-23
       32       20            20     33.0  1.2e-43
       32       20            10     16.5  3.4e-22
       32       60            10      5.5  7.0e-08
       32       60            60     33.0  1.2e-43
design (ack on every upstream frame, both lanes, L=32) at busy profile: each dn_u frame covered by 116 acks

== Ack bytes alone, busy profile
design 420 B/s, proposed 79 B/s

== Section length prefixes downstream, as share of the 16,000 B/s state budget (busy)
192 B/s of kind+length = 1.2% of stateBudget

== Intern table (design §4.4: per connection, append-only, cap 4096, no transient marker)
  1 new strings/s server-wide broadcast -> table full after  68.3 min
  5 new strings/s server-wide broadcast -> table full after  13.7 min
 20 new strings/s server-wide broadcast -> table full after   3.4 min
cap 4096 x t.string(20) x 100 connections, one direction: up to 18.0 MB server memory
cap 4096 x t.string(200) x 100 connections, one direction: up to 91.8 MB server memory

== Handshake HELLO size (design §4.5) by definition count, hash widths 32/64 bit
n= 20 hash=32b  HELLO    91 B   (needed when hashes match: 6 B)
n= 20 hash=64b  HELLO   175 B   (needed when hashes match: 10 B)
n=100 hash=32b  HELLO   411 B   (needed when hashes match: 6 B)
n=100 hash=64b  HELLO   815 B   (needed when hashes match: 10 B)
n=300 hash=32b  HELLO  1211 B   (needed when hashes match: 6 B)
n=300 hash=64b  HELLO  2415 B   (needed when hashes match: 10 B)

== Request ids (design §5.5: u16 per request and per reply)
implicit request id (both sides count reliable requests): saves 16 bits per request
reply id as offset into the in-flight window (cap 16): 4 bits instead of 16

== timestamped (design §5.6: 1 B sub-tick offset per event)
state 20 Hz, frames 60 Hz: frame index within tick = 2 bits per frame; per-event offset = 8 bits per event
state 30 Hz, frames 60 Hz: frame index within tick = 1 bits per frame; per-event offset = 8 bits per event
state 60 Hz, frames 60 Hz: frame index within tick = 0 bits per frame; per-event offset = 8 bits per event

== Notify in-flight ring per viewer (design §5.2; research says 64 entries, ack covers 33)
 50 records/frame, 64 entries: buffer u16   6.2 KB, Luau array   50.0 KB per viewer
 50 records/frame, 33 entries: buffer u16   3.2 KB, Luau array   25.8 KB per viewer
200 records/frame, 64 entries: buffer u16  25.0 KB, Luau array  200.0 KB per viewer
200 records/frame, 33 entries: buffer u16  12.9 KB, Luau array  103.1 KB per viewer
